{"text": "PHILIP MORRIS U. S. A.\nINTER-OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\nRichmond, Virginia\n\nTo: + Mr. W. Houck Date: September 6, 1985\nFrom: C. L. McKay\n\nSubject: . Preliminary Results from the Extended Testing of DATA 100mm\nMenthol and Nonmenthol Cigarettes\n\nDATA 100mm menthol (POL 0059) and nonmenthol (POL 0060) cigarettes preset\non the thinnest bar were evaluated by cross-sections of both full flavor\nand low tar menthol and nonmenthol smokers, respectively. Each panelist\ncompleted two evaluations during the study. The menthol cigarettes had\nBenson and Hedges filler and aftercut and the nonmenthol cigarettes had\nMarlboro filler and aftercut. Both types of DATA cigarettes had the\nspecial DATA filter and the bar logo imprinted in gold on white tipping.\nThe menthol cigarettes delivered between 6mg and l\u00e9ng FIC tar and the\nnonmenthol cigarettes delivered between 5mg and 16mg FIC tar depending on\nwhere the cigarettes were set between the endpoints. The DATA 85mm\nnonmenthol cigarettes had Marlboro filler and aftercut and delivered\nbetween 7mg and 15mg FTC tar.\n\nAt the completion of this study, panelists were given a choice of an\nadditional carton of their own brand or another carton of DATA, Forty-\nfour percent of the menthol 100nm smokers and forty-one percent of the\nnonmenthoT 100mm smokers chose to receive an additional carton of DATA.\nIn the previous 85mm nonmenthol extended study (POL 0053), thirty-four\npercent of the smokers who completed both evaluations chose to receive an\nadditional carton of DATA.* The percentages of usable ballots returned in\nthe three tests were comparable. Based on the final evaluations from\nthose panel ists who completed both evaluations, the following coments can\ne made.\n\nOverall, the 100mm smokers gave the DATA cigarettes higher acceptability\nratings after extended smoking compared to the ratings given by 85nm\nnonmenthol smokers to DATA 85mm nonmenthol cigarettes (Table I). Slightly\nhigher acceptability ratings were given to the DATA 100mm menthol\ncigarettes compared to the 100mm nonmenthol DATA cigarettes.\n\n\u201cTechnical Report, titled \"Extended Testing of DATA 85mm Nonmenthol\n\nCigarettes,\" by Cheryl Mckay, dated August 27, 1985, Accession No. 85-177.\n\n6esosetepe", "words": [{"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 290, "y0": 118, "x1": 332, "y1": 129, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 339, "y0": 118, "x1": 382, "y1": 129, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "U.", "x0": 397, "y0": 118, "x1": 409, "y1": 129, "conf": 88.0}, {"text": "S.", "x0": 419, "y0": 118, "x1": 431, "y1": 129, "conf": 75.0}, {"text": "A.", "x0": 440, "y0": 118, "x1": 452, "y1": 129, "conf": 83.0}, {"text": "INTER-OFFICE", "x0": 176, "y0": 146, "x1": 339, "y1": 157, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "CORRESPONDENCE", "x0": 376, "y0": 146, "x1": 568, "y1": 158, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Richmond,", "x0": 311, "y0": 174, "x1": 373, "y1": 187, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Virginia", "x0": 383, "y0": 174, "x1": 440, "y1": 188, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "To:", "x0": 89, "y0": 232, "x1": 108, "y1": 243, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "+", "x0": 156, "y0": 239, "x1": 159, "y1": 242, "conf": 45.0}, {"text": "Mr.", "x0": 175, "y0": 232, "x1": 194, "y1": 242, "conf": 45.0}, {"text": "W.", "x0": 204, "y0": 232, "x1": 215, "y1": 242, "conf": 73.0}, {"text": "Houck", "x0": 225, "y0": 231, "x1": 261, "y1": 243, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Date:", "x0": 441, "y0": 232, "x1": 474, "y1": 243, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "September", "x0": 491, "y0": 232, "x1": 555, "y1": 246, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "6,", "x0": 563, "y0": 233, "x1": 574, "y1": 245, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "1985", "x0": 585, "y0": 233, "x1": 611, "y1": 243, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "From:", "x0": 90, "y0": 260, "x1": 122, "y1": 271, "conf": 4.0}, {"text": "C.", "x0": 176, "y0": 260, "x1": 187, "y1": 270, "conf": 51.0}, {"text": "L.", "x0": 198, "y0": 260, "x1": 208, "y1": 270, "conf": 80.0}, {"text": "McKay", "x0": 218, "y0": 260, "x1": 253, "y1": 273, "conf": 87.0}, {"text": "Subject:", "x0